      "reasons": [
        "Peer ranges admit the video-utils pins (Svelte 5.57.1, Skeleton 5.0.1) and there is no Effect dependency, so it is not blocked on TIN-5716.",
        "Its peer dependency fft.js 4.0.4 is not in web/package.json or web/pnpm-lock.yaml; adding it is a root-owned change.",
        "A Bazel-only package is absent from the pnpm install that `pnpm build` and `pnpm check` (the accepted gates) use, so importing it from web/src would break those gates until root decides how the two paths coexist.",
        "The source archive is a private GitHub API tarball: Bazel needs a credential helper to fetch it, which the hosted CI job does not have.",
        "Use is unproven: web/src/lib/components/review/SpectrogramView.svelte renders the server-produced low-register spectrogram; the module's DSP core is a 16 kHz mel/PCEN demo pipeline and its behaviour near 32 Hz was not measured."
      ],
      "root_changes_needed": [
        "web/package.json + web/pnpm-lock.yaml: fft.js 4.0.4",
        "web/src: import @xoxd/spectrogram",
        "decision on Bazel-only packages versus the pnpm gates",
        "CI credential for the private source archive"
      ]
